          "body": "Could you try changing ItemDefinitionProviderImpl.getQNodeDefinition() to catch a ConstraintViolationException instead of RepositoryException? \n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=reschke",
            "name": "reschke",
            "key": "reschke",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677"
            },
            "displayName": "Julian Reschke",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "created": "2007-08-30T11:19:15.326+0000",
          "updated": "2007-08-30T11:19:15.326+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12377122/comment/12523884",
          "id": "12523884",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=drauschenbach",
            "name": "drauschenbach",
            "key": "drauschenbach",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "David Rauschenbach",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Los_Angeles"
          },
          "body": "That wouldn't change the flow. I'm having a ConstraintViolationException thrown, so it'd get caught the same way. The exception message is \"no matching child node definition found for {}Inbox\". I guess that's my ultimate problem, that my effective node type object has empty named and unnamed node definition arrays. But those values are coming straight from the in-memory transient repository, through my SPI bridge, so I don't see where the values could get dropped.\n\nNevertheless, if those arrays are empty (maybe due to a counterpart flaw in spi2jcr?), this flow still seems to be invalid, since an SPI can return anything, and it should not trigger a crash.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=drauschenbach",
            "name": "drauschenbach",
            "key": "drauschenbach",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "David Rauschenbach",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Los_Angeles"
          },
          "created": "2007-08-30T17:05:04.474+0000",
          "updated": "2007-08-30T17:05:04.474+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12377122/comment/12523904",
          "id": "12523904",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=reschke",
            "name": "reschke",
            "key": "reschke",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=reschke&avatarId=52677",
